{
  "reasons": {
    "color-contrast": "Token level, not per component: status colours (--red, --green, --blue, the accent, a project colour) carry text on their own tints or on --bg-1 (2.8–4.4:1), and the dark danger button is white on #cc6b6b (3.6:1). The fix is the --amber-text pattern for every tone (--red-text, --green-text, --blue-text, accent text), tinted pairs in the tokens.config.json contrast gate, and a darker dark --red for fills; a design decision across app and lib, tracked as a follow-up to DS-16.",
    "scrollable-region-focusable": "The sample content of these stories is plain text, so the scrolling dialog body / panel body has nothing focusable. Real dialogs and panels hold controls; Chromium (130+) and Firefox make such scrollers keyboard-focusable, Safari does not. Decide in the overlay work whether ath-dialog / ath-panel set tabindex=0 while they overflow."
  },
